# Virtual environment — regenerates from uv.lock via `uv sync`
.venv/

# Python cache
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# OS / OneDrive files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Secrets — EDGAR_IDENTITY and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY live here, never in git.
# .env.example IS committed as the template.
.env

# Claude Code persistent memory (local only)
memory/

# --- Generated pipeline artifacts ---
# data/raw/ is deliberately NOT ignored below in spirit, but it is large and
# re-fetchable. See DATA.md: the cache is precious locally (never re-hit EDGAR)
# but it is a *copy* of public EDGAR documents, so it does not belong in git.
data/raw/

# Extracted sections regenerate from data/raw/ deterministically and for free.
data/sections/

# data/ledger/ IS COMMITTED. It was ignored on the same "it regenerates"
# reasoning as data/sections/, and for the ledger that reasoning is wrong:
#
#   - data/ledger/facts/ is model output. It cost $4.52 to produce and a re-run
#     would not reproduce it byte-for-byte, so it is the ONLY artifact in this
#     project that cannot be regenerated. It is also the audit record of what the
#     model actually returned, which is what makes every quote in the ledger
#     checkable after the fact.
#   - The rest of data/ledger/ derives from it deterministically, but derives
#     from nothing at all in a clean checkout, because data/raw/ and
#     data/sections/ are both ignored.
#
# 904 KB, and it is the analytical substance of the project. It belongs in git.

# Final deliverables regenerate from data/ledger/
output/

# Per-run logs
logs/
*.log
